[83.598596, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1mCreated Files\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[3m1. converter.py\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[KA temperature conversion module with:\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2022 \u001b[1mModule-level docstring\u001b[22m explaining the Kelvin/Rankine relationship and their use cases\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2022 \u001b[1mkelvin_to_rankine()\u001b[22m function with complete Google-style docstring including:\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u25e6 Args: parameter description with constraints\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u25e6 Returns: return type and meaning\r\r\n\u001b[5G\u001b[KRaises: ValueError for negative temps, TypeError for non-numeric input\r\r\n\u001b[5G\u001b[KExample: three doctest examples showing typical usage\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2022 \u001b[1mrankine_to_kelvin()\u001b[22m function with identical documentation structure\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u2022 Both functions include input validation for type and range\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1m\u001b[3m2. show_help.py\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KA simple script that imports the converter module and prints its help documentation.\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[1mOutput\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[KThe `help\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[E\u001b[E\u001b[E\u001b[E\u001b[E\u001b[E\u001b[21G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;248m7 \u2026\u001b[39m           \u001b[33m\u26a1auto \u00b7 \u001b[36m\u001b[2m[core] \u001b[39manthropic-vertex/claude-sonnet-4-5 \u00b7  9% \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;35m\u25b0\u25b1\u25b1\u25b1\u25b1\u25b1\u25b1\u25b1\u001b[39m\u001b7\u001b[2;77H\u001b[38;5;210m\u2584\u001b[38;5;210m\u2580\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2588\u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;216m\u2584\u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;216m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2580\u001b[38;5;222m\u2588\u001b[38;5;222m\u2580\u001b[0m\u001b[3;77H\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588\u001b[38;5;210m\u2580\u001b[38;5;210m\u2588 \u001b[38;5;